9
00:00:19,128 --> 00:00:21,775
Across fixed evaluation gates: nine of nine

10
00:00:21,810 --> 00:00:24,682
named falls and sixty of sixty randomized falls.

11
00:00:37,735 --> 00:00:39,283
Next: fall recovery.

12
00:00:39,465 --> 00:00:41,485
A safety line catches the initial loss of

13
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:44,074
traction, the controller uses rope tension to

14
00:00:44,109 --> 00:00:46,965
recover its stance, and a learned get-up returns

15
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,706
the robot to its feet so the route

16
00:00:48,741 --> 00:00:49,662
can continue.

17
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:03,836
For cliffs, the rappel policy coordinates

18
00:01:03,871 --> 00:01:05,508
braking with foot placement on a

19
00:01:05,543 --> 00:01:07,114
sixty-five-degree face.

20
00:01:07,470 --> 00:01:09,583
Watch the brake hand hold tension while the

21
00:01:09,618 --> 00:01:12,381
feet search for stable contacts: a two-meter

22
00:01:12,416 --> 00:01:14,568
